00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:32.640
As I was saying, the reason Antonio Ciseri&nbsp;
took 20 years to paint this work is because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:38.560
he was an extreme perfectionist. He was a man&nbsp;
trained in the academic tradition of Florence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:43.280
and his contemporaries described him as&nbsp;
a painter of Raphaelesque precision with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:48.640
almost photographic effects. Each of his works&nbsp;
went through years of preparatory studies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:51.760
sketches, corrections, and refinements.

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:55.280
But in the case of the Ecce&nbsp;
Homo there was something more.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:06:01.360
This work was commissioned by the Italian&nbsp;
government in 1871, when Ciseri was already fifty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:06.880
years old and one of the most respected religious&nbsp;
painters in Europe. At that point this was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:13.040
in many ways, the commission of his life, and also&nbsp;
the opportunity to create his definitive work.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:15.440
During the two decades following the commission,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:19.520
while painting portraits of kings and&nbsp;
distinguished figures to earn a living,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:24.960
he kept returning to this painting again&nbsp;
and again. Adjusting the light, refining the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:31.520
garments of his protagonists, and perfecting every&nbsp;
detail of a scene he wanted to be unsurpassable.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:39.280
Antonio Ciseri died in March 1891, in Florence,&nbsp;
with the work just completed. The Ecce Homo was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:45.120
the final point of his career, and the last&nbsp;
image of an entire life dedicated to painting.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:51.040
Something worth mentioning is that this work&nbsp;
measures almost 4 meters wide by 3 meters tall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:56.160
making it a monumental piece and the&nbsp;
largest of his entire career. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:59.600
I would love to know your opinion&nbsp;
on whether you think dedicating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:04.320
20 years to a single painting is&nbsp;
excessive, or if on the contrary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:09.680
you believe it is natural for an artist to&nbsp;
turn their masterpiece into a lifelong work.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:13.200
I will be reading your opinions&nbsp;
in the comments. As always,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:21.200
thank you for watching the video until the&nbsp;
end, and I will see you in the next video.

